`copy_` on the same volume as a ceiling and got 6.77 TB/s, so this is at HBM bandwidth. I swept tile heights (1/2/4/8 rows), warp counts, cache modifiers, and a persistent-CU variant; nothing beat the simple config, which confirmed there was no headroom left here.\n- **Small batch (1–79 rows)** — the kernel itself finishes in well under a microsecond, so time was *entirely* host-side launch cost. Triton's per-call dispatch (argument binder, cache-key hashing, grid canonicalization) measured ~8µs against ~4µs for the raw launch. Caching the compiled binary and invoking it directly took these from 16µs to **5.5µs**, a ~3x win that had nothing to do with the GPU.\n\nThe fast path runs the *same compiled binary with the same arguments* — only Triton's host-side dispatch layer is skipped. Work still lands on the caller's stream inside the timed region; nothing is cached across calls or deferred.\n\n## Robustness\n\nSince the real score comes from a clean tree on a different GPU, I tested beyond the 7 workloads: non-default streams, CUDA-graph capture, non-contiguous inputs, `inference_mode`, `enable_grad`, and shapes straddling the tile-size threshold. All pass. The stream is resolved per-call rather than captured at build time so side-stream and graph capture enqueue correctly, and anything the cached binary wasn't built for (wrong dtype, strided, mismatched shapes, `hidden_size != 2048`) falls back to a general path.\n\nOne thing worth flagging: **the harness reports 60µs/47µs for the two large shapes where I measure 22µs/28µs.** That gap is real and reproducible — the harness times calls in isolation, and per-call event timing on this GPU carries a fixed ~11µs launch/drain tail that back-to-back timing amortizes away. I re-tuned specifically against isolated-call latency to check whether a different config would hide it; the ranking was unchanged, so the tail is dispatch overhead rather than something the kernel can address. I'd expect the same offset on the scoring run.","ttft_ms":303273,"ttft_stream_ms":303271,"time_to_request_ms":139,"type":"result","duration_ms":1056989,"uuid":"518f023b-e93c-4005-8649-ba0f4f282ec0"}
